questionText:
Consider a C program that declares the following local variables inside main():

int a[10];
double b;
char *p = malloc(25 * sizeof(char));

The system uses 4 bytes for an int, 8 bytes for a double, and 1 byte per char. Each heap allocation incurs an 8‑byte bookkeeping header. What is the total amount of memory (in bytes) that will be reserved for these three variables during execution?
